{"The narrowed locking in `bleveBackend.BuildIndex` removes mutual exclusion around index creation for a given key; if multiple callers race to build the same index, you may end up doing duplicate work or overwriting the cache entry\u2014consider a per-key lock or double-checked cache lookup before/after building to avoid concurrent builds for the same namespace/resource": 0.799044668674469, "Cache writes are now locked but reads appear unsynchronized, which can cause a data race on b.cache - the early read (`if idx, ok := b.cache[key]; ok { ... }`) is not protected while the write is locked, causing a Go data race when BuildIndex is called concurrently": 0.8435494303703308, "Moving `Init` into `NewResourceServer` means server construction now blocks on index/watcher initialization and can fail; consider whether this needs a bounded timeout or a background goroutine so that a slow index build doesn't prevent the process from starting or make it harder to surface a partially-initialized state": 0.5765778422355652}